# Design system

Canonical primitives: `apps/hospital-portal-web/src/components/ui/` (shadcn/ui + Radix, Lucide, `cn()` in `src/lib/utils.ts`). Reuse before creating anything.

## Reuse before create

Search, in order: `src/components/ui` → owning domain kit → existing usages → shared helpers. Prefer composition. Do not duplicate Button, Card, Dialog, Sheet, AlertDialog, Table, Input, Select/Combobox, Tabs, Badge, Tooltip, Popover, Calendar, form controls, or toast primitives.

Canonical choices: Dialog=`ui/dialog.tsx`; side panel=`ui/sheet.tsx`; confirmation=`ui/alert-dialog.tsx` or existing ConfirmationDialog; IP/ward/OT=`IpOverlayDialog`; new Tabs=`ui/radix-tabs.tsx`; icons=Lucide; toasts=`react-hot-toast`; staff chrome=`Sidebar` + `TopNav`; permissions=`PermissionGate` + `ProtectedRoute`.

## Counsellor module as the UX benchmark

The existing Counsellor/Counselling module is the **canonical reference for the level of UI polish, information hierarchy, density, workflow clarity, dialogs/sheets, loading/empty/error states, recording/session workspace patterns, and overall staff-product finish**.

For every **new or changed staff UI/UX request**, compare the target work against the existing Counsellor implementation before designing or implementing. Use `apps/hospital-portal-web/src/components/counsellors-desk` and its related counselling routes/API usage as the primary reference. Inspect only the **smallest relevant representative screen/component**, not the entire counselling module.

Reference means: match the quality, consistency, interaction principles, hierarchy, spacing discipline, state handling, and polish. Do **not** copy counselling-specific business logic, colors, terminology, permissions, workflow states, or domain components into another domain unless they are already canonical/shared.

If the target domain has an intentional established scoped visual system (IP target, auth, patient portal, etc.), preserve that domain system while matching the Counsellor module's quality bar.

## Scoped visual systems

Keep existing scoped systems such as `.ip-target`, `.counselling-session`, `.auth-oc`, and patient portal UX. Do not create a new token file or another global primary color. Do not spread counselling session chrome globally.

## Competing stacks

Do not add Headless UI, fixed custom overlay stacks, sonner, react-select, Material Symbols, TanStack Table, socket.io-client, or another design system without explicit approval. Do not paste Figma-generated Tailwind as a new component language.

## Layout and shared components

Follow existing App Router layouts. Desktop workstation efficiency is primary for staff workflows. Search all consumers before changing shared `ui/*` or shared domain primitives.
